ch](#)\n\n. 2024:2799:1-11.\n\ndoi: 10.1007/978-1-0716-3830-9\\_1.\n\n# Spectrum of NMDA Receptor Variants in Neurodevelopmental Disorders and Epilepsy\n\n[Cathrine E Gjerulfsen](/?term=Gjerulfsen+CE&cauthor_id=38727899)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Epilepsy Genetics and Personalized Medicine, Danish Epilepsy Centre, Dianalund, Denmark.\") , [Ilona Krey](/?term=Krey+I&cauthor_id=38727899)  [2](#full-view-affiliation-2 \"Institute of Human Genetics, University of Leipzig Medical Center, Leipzig, Germany.\") , [Chiara Klöckner](/?term=Kl%C3%B6ckner+C&cauthor_id=38727899)  [2](#full-view-affiliation-2 \"Institute of Human Genetics, University of Leipzig Medical Center, Leipzig, Germany.\") , [Guido Rubboli](/?term=Rubboli+G&cauthor_id=38727899)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Epilepsy Genetics and Personalized Medicine, Danish Epilepsy Centre, Dianalund, Denmark.\")   [3](#full-view-affiliation-3 \"Institute of Clinical Medicine, University of Copenhagen, Copenhagen, Denmark.\") , [Johannes R Lemke](/?term=Lemke+JR&cauthor_id=38727899)  [2](#full-view-affiliation-2 \"Institute of Human Genetics, University of Leipzig Medical Center, Leipzig, Germany.\") , [Rikke S Møller](/?term=M%C3%B8ller+RS&cauthor_id=38727899)  [4](#full-view-affiliation-4 \"Department of Epilepsy Genetics and Personalized Medicine, Danish Epilepsy Centre, Dianalund, Denmark. rimo@filadelfia.dk.\")   [5](#full-view-affiliation-5 \"Department of Regional Health Research, Faculty of Health Sciences, University of Southern Denmark, Odense, Denmark. rimo@filadelfia.dk.\")\n\nAffiliations Expand\n\n### Affiliations\n\n-   1 Department of Epilepsy Genetics and Personalized Medicine, Danish Epilepsy Centre, Dianalund, Denmark.\n-   2 Institute of Human Genetics, University of Leipzig Medical Center, Leipzig, Germany.\n-   3 Institute of Clinical Medicine, University of Copenhagen, Copenhagen, Denmark.\n-   4 Department of Epilepsy Genetics and Personalized Medicine, Danish Epilepsy Centre, Dianalund, Denmark. rimo@filadelfia.dk.\n-   5 Department of Regional Health Research, Faculty of Health Sciences, University of Southern Denmark, Odense, Denmark. rimo@filadelfia.dk.\n\n-   PMID: **38727899**\n-   DOI: [10.1007/978-1-0716-3830-9\\_1](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-0716-3830-9_1)\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\nReview\n\n# Spectrum of NMDA Receptor Variants in Neurodevelopmental Disorders and Epilepsy\n\nCathrine E Gjerulfsen et al. Methods Mol Biol. 2024.\n\nShow details\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat Abstract PubMed PMID\n\nMethods Mol Biol\n\nActions\n\n-   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Methods+Mol+Biol%22%5Bjour%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n-   [Search in NLM Catalog](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/nlmcatalog?term=%22Methods+Mol+Biol%22%5BTitle+Abbreviation%5D)\n-   [Add to Search](#)\n\n. 2024:2799:1-11.\n\ndoi: 10.1007/978-1-0716-3830-9\\_1.\n\n### Authors\n\n[Cathrine E Gjerulfsen](/?term=Gjerulfsen+CE&cauthor_id=38727899)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Epilepsy Genetics and Personalized Medicine, Danish Epilepsy Centre, Dianalund, Denmark.\") , [Ilona Krey](/?term=Krey+I&cauthor_id=38727899)  [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Institute of Human Genetics, University of Leipzig Medical Center, Leipzig, Germany.\") , [Chiara Klöckner](/?term=Kl%C3%B6ckner+C&cauthor_id=38727899)  [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Institute of Human Genetics, University of Leipzig Medical Center, Leipzig, Germany.\") , [Guido Rubboli](/?term=Rubboli+G&cauthor_id=38727899)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Epilepsy Genetics and Personalized Medicine, Danish Epilepsy Centre, Dianalund, Denmark.\")   [3](#short-view-affiliation-3 \"Institute of Clinical Medicine, University of Copenhagen, Copenhagen, Denmark.\") , [Johannes R Lemke](/?term=Lemke+JR&cauthor_id=38727899)  [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Institute of Human Genetics, University of Leipzig Medical Center, Leipzig, Germany.\") , [Rikke S Møller](/?term=M%C3%B8ller+RS&cauthor_id=38727899)  [4](#short-view-affiliation-4 \"Department of Epilepsy Genetics and Personalized Medicine, Danish Epilepsy Centre, Dianalund, Denmark. rimo@filadelfia.dk.\")   [5](#short-view-affiliation-5 \"Department of Regional Health Research, Faculty of Health Sciences, University of Southern Denmark, Odense, Denmark. rimo@filadelfia.dk.\")\n\n### Affiliations\n\n-   1 Department of Epilepsy Genetics and Personalized Medicine, Danish Epilepsy Centre, Dianalund, Denmark.\n-   2 Institute of Human Genetics, University of Leipzig Medical Center, Leipzig, Germany.\n-   3 Institute of Clinical Medicine, University of Copenhagen, Copenhagen, Denmark.\n-   4 Department of Epilepsy Genetics and Personalized Medicine, Danish Epilepsy Centre, Dianalund, Denmark. rimo@filadelfia.dk.\n-   5 Department of Regional Health Research, Faculty of Health Sciences, University of Southern Denmark, Odense, Denmark. rimo@filadelfia.dk.\n\n-   PMID: **38727899**\n-   DOI: [10.1007/978-1-0716-3830-9\\_1](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-0716-3830-9_1)\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\nFull text links Cite\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat AbstractPubMedPMID\n\n## Abstract\n\nN-methyl-D-aspartate receptors (NMDAR) are ligand-gated ion channels mediating excitatory neurotransmission and are important for normal brain development, cognitive abilities, and motor functions. Pathogenic variants in the Glutamate receptor Ionotropic N-methyl-D-aspartate (GRIN) genes (GRIN1, GRIN2A-D) encoding NMDAR subunits have been associated with a wide spectrum of neurodevelopmental disorders and epilepsies ranging from treatable focal epilepsies to devastating early-onset developmental and epileptic encephalopathies. Genetic variants in NMDA receptor genes can cause a range of complex alterations to receptor properties resulting in various degrees of loss-of-function, gain-of-function, or mixtures thereof. Understanding how genetic variants affect the function of the receptors, therefore, represents an important first step in the ongoing development towards targeted therapies. Currently, targeted treatment options for GRIN-related diseases are limited. However, treatment with memantine has been reported to significantly reduce seizure frequency in a few individuals with developmental and epileptic encephalopathies harboring de novo gain-of-function GRIN2A missense variants, and supplementary treatment with L-serine has been associated with improved motor and cognitive performance as well as reduced seizure frequency in patients with GRIN2B loss-of-function missense variants as well as GRIN2A and GRIN2B null variants.\n\n**Keywords:** Channelopathy; Epilepsy genetics; Epileptic encephalopathy; NMDA receptors; Precision medicine.\n\n© 2024. The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Science+Business Media, LLC, part of Springer Nature.\n\n[PubMed Disclaimer](/disclaimer/)\n\n## References\n\n1.  1.  Scheffer IE, Liao J (2020) Deciphering the concepts behind “Epileptic encephalopathy” and “Developmental and epileptic encephalopathy”. Eur J Paediatr Neurol 24:11–14. [https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejpn.2019.12.023](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejpn.2019.12.023) - [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejpn.2019.12.023) - [PubMed](/31926847/)\n2.  1.  Benke TA, Krey I, Camp CR et al (2021) Clinical and therapeutic significance of genetic variation in the GRIN gene family encoding NMDARs. Neuropharmacology 199:108805. [https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuropharm.2021.108805](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuropharm.2021.108805) - [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuropharm.2021.108805) - [PubMed](/34560056/) - [PMC](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/8525401/)\n3.  1.  Hanada T (2020) Ionotropic glutamate receptors in epilepsy: a review focusing on AMPA and NMDA receptors. Biomol Ther 10(3):464. [https://doi.org/10.3390/biom10030464](https://doi.org/10.3390/biom10030464) - [DOI](https://doi.org/10.3390/biom10030464)\n4.  1.  Laube B, Kuhse J, Betz H (1998) Evidence for a tetrameric structure of recombinant NMDA receptors. J Neurosci 18(8):2954–2961. [https://doi.org/10.1523/JNEUROSCI.18-08-02954.199](https://doi.org/10.1523/JNEUROSCI.18-08-02954.199) - [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1523/jneurosci.18-08-02954.199) - [PubMed](/9526012/) - [PMC](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/6792599/)\n5.  1.  Endele S, Geider K, Popp B et al (2010) Mutations in GRIN2A and GRIN2B encoding regulatory subunits of NMDA receptors cause variable neurodevelopmental phenotypes. Nat Genet 42(11):1021–1026. [https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.677](https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.677) - [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.677) - [PubMed](/20890276/)\n\nShow all 29 references\n\n## Publication types\n\n-   Review\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Review%22%5Bpt%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Review)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n\n## MeSH terms\n\n-   Epilepsy\\* / drug therapy\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Epilepsy%2Fdrug+therapy%22%5BMAJR%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Epilepsy)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Epilepsy\\* / genetics\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Epilepsy%2Fgenetics%22%5BMAJR%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Epilepsy)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Genetic Predisposition to Disease\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Genetic+Predisposition+to+Disease%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Genetic+Predisposition+to+Disease)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Genetic Variation\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Genetic+Variation%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Genet