{"type":"text","timestamp":1778614250782,"sessionID":"ses_1e25a7618ffeAfAyFghsAo42su","part":{"id":"prt_e1dab910f001uBVOzqtk1EBaTU","messageID":"msg_e1dab8923001ktWFkAH6gBLBQZ","sessionID":"ses_1e25a7618ffeAfAyFghsAo42su","type":"text","text":"Done. Here's a summary of what I did for **issue #9930**:\n\n### Actions taken\n1. **Verified all PMIDs** from the references provided in the issue:\n   - Santos-Gómez et al. Hum Mol Genet. 2021 → **PMID:33043365**\n   - Santos-Gómez et al. Int J Mol Sci. 2021 → **PMID:34884460**\n   - Gjerulfsen et al. Methods Mol Biol. 2024 → **PMID:38727899**\n   - Benke et al. Neuropharmacology. 2021 → **PMID:34560056**\n\n2. **Checked out, edited, and checked in** `MONDO:1060138` and added 3 new EXACT synonyms with verified citations:\n   - `grinpathies` [PMID:34884460]\n   - `GRIN-related encephalopathy` [PMID:33043365, PMID:34560056, PMID:38727899]\n   - `GRIN-related neurodevelopmental disorder` [PMID:33043365, PMID:34560056, PMID:34884460, PMID:38727899]\n\n3. **Added a term tracker item** for issue #9930.\n\n4. **Ran `make NORM`** via ODK docker and committed the normalized file.\n\n### Key decision\nThe requester asked for **\"GRINopathies\"**. Curator `@MeeSiing` asked for clarification on the correct spelling (\"GRINpathies\" vs \"grinpathies\"), but no response was received. I checked the literature: **PMID:34884460** explicitly uses the lowercase form **\"grinpathies\"** (\"GRIN-related disorders (GRD), the so-called grinpathies\"). No published source supports the \"GRINopathies\" spelling. Therefore, I used the literature-backed form.\n\n### Files created\n- `ISSUE_COMMENTS.md` — status update for the originating issue\n- `PR_COMMENTS.md` — detailed description of changes and rationale\n\nBoth are in the repo root and ready for you to feed back.","time":{"start":1778614243599,"end":1778614250781}}}
